Maya (Presales): Quick ask for the Acme POC tomorrow — 1-page runbook showing: streaming SDK (Node + Go), example function/tool-call, structured JSON output check, handshake cURL for ephemeral tokens, and a short security Q&A (KMS, log retention, SOC2 link). Can someone assemble a compact draft by EOD?

Jon (Eng): I can do a tight draft. Confirm hosted EU region, ephemeral tokens required, and include a quantized fallback?

Lina (Sales): Yep EU, ephemeral tokens preferred. They want logs off by default. Finance will fill pricing placeholders.

Jon (Eng): Draft bullets + tiny snippets: 
- Goal: demo streaming chat + function calls + schema validation.
- Env: hosted (eu), primary model r-infer-2, fallback r-infer-2-quant-small.
- Auth: short-lived token or API key; example token exchange omitted for brevity. KMS for keys; TLS required. Logs disabled by default.

Node snippet:
```js
const c = new Redwood({ token: process.env.RW_TOKEN, region: 'eu' });
const s = c.chat.stream({ model: 'r-infer-2' });
s.on('event', e => {
  if (e.type === 'function_call') {
    if (e.schemaHash !== 'sha256:abc') return;
    fetch('https://hooks.acme/exec', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(e.payload) });
  }
});
```

Go snippet:
```go
cli := redwood.NewClient(os.Getenv("RW_TOKEN"))
stream := cli.ChatStream(ctx, redwood.ChatParams{Model: "r-infer-2", Region: "eu"})
for ev := range stream.Events() {
  if ev.Type == redwood.EventFunctionCall && ev.SchemaHash == "sha256:abc" {
    http.Post("https://hooks.acme/exec", "application/json", bytes.NewReader(ev.Payload))
  }
}
```

Handshake cURL (SSE):
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_TOKEN" -H "Accept: text/event-stream" "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams/chat?model=r-infer-2&region=eu"

Structured output: validate against a compact JSON Schema on receive, recommend SDK schema hook.

Operational knobs: batching 10-25ms, KV prefix cache enabled. Fallback: route to r-infer-2-quant-small when queue latency >80ms or GPU util >75%.

Security Q&A (short):
- Data residency: EU-only endpoints for this POC; Private/VPC available for Dedicated.
- Encryption: TLS in transit; KMS-managed keys at rest (HSM optional).
- Logs: inference logs not retained by default; retention configurable with consent.
- Compliance: SOC2 attestation link will be added by legal; DPA available.

Jon (Eng): Quick troubleshooting bullets: 401 -> check token/clock skew; SSE stalls -> missing Accept header/CORS; tool call failures -> webhook TLS or IP allowlist.

Lina (Sales): Ill chase finance and legal for SOC2 URL and pricing numbers. Tag @Maya when final.

